Nope. Not a chance. BTW you can't wish for one either. The only way to get one
is to pick it up.

A WoW is a convenience for wishes as you get up to 7 of them out of one and
it's virtually guaranteed to work. However there are several other ways 
potentially to get wishes. And the objects can be wished for and even stacked:

1) djinns from blessed smoky potions.
2) djinns from blessed magic lamps
3) water demons from fountains. This is a dangerous course of action due to 
   lots ot potential bad effects. But fountains are plentiful throughout the
   dungeon.
4) Sitting on thrones. Just put away your money (You notice you have no gold),
   rings (massive surge of electricity), and may want to consider having
   some way to restore attributes handy (blessed unicorn horn is great for 
   that)

Finally every game has one guaranteed WoW, in the Castle. But it's a tough
road getting there.

As for using wishes, gearing up is the first priority with armor first then
weaponry (which of course you can pray for). Then I usually work on stats.
When I running a wizard (my character of choice) the Helm of Brilliance is
my #2 wish item after SDSM.

Good luck.

